course: dictionary
lesson: 8052
title: Practise before you perform
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To rehearse means to practise something before you do it in front of other people, such as a play, a song, a dance or a speech. A practice session for a performance is called a rehearsal.
explain: You can rehearse out loud, or quietly in your head, by going over what you will say or do until you feel ready. «Stunt performers are trained professionals who rehearse with safety teams» before any real stunt is attempted.
explain: Look for clues in the sentence. «The band cannot rehearse full songs if people do not turn up» tells you that rehearsing needs people to practise with. Ask yourself: is this about getting ready for something? If so, rehearse probably means practise.
fact: To rehearse means to practise before a performance.
fact: «Rehearse your lines» means practise the words you will say in a play.
fact: A «dress rehearsal» is a full practice, done as if it were the real show.
fact: «A rehearsal is a practice session for a performance.»
fact: Schools rehearse fire drills so that everyone knows what to do if there is a real fire.
exercise: «A rehearsal is a practice session for a performance.» What does rehearse mean? | Run away quickly | *Practise before doing it in front of people | Forget everything you know | Eat a big meal
exercise: In a story, a child rehearses what to say to a teacher. What is she doing? | Hiding from the teacher | *Practising her words in her head before she speaks | Going on holiday | Singing loudly
exercise: «The band cannot rehearse full songs if people do not turn up.» What does this tell you? | Bands do not need to practise | Songs are never sung | *Rehearsing needs people to practise with | Turning up is not important
test: Which phrase means a full practice, done as if it were the real show? | A loud whisper | A curtain call | *A dress rehearsal | A fire escape
test: Which word is the noun form of rehearse? | rehearsed | stunt | *rehearsal | curtain
exam: «The curtain call is the bows at the end, and it is rehearsed, often with the lead bowing last.» What does rehearsed mean here? | Hidden | Forgotten | *Practised before the show | Cancelled
